#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:5
msgid "Project"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost server plugin (`mattermost-ai`) that integrates LLM providers."
" Go 1.26 backend + React/TypeScript webapp (Node 24.11)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:9
msgid "Commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:11
msgid "`make help` lists every documented target with a one-line description."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:13
msgid ""
"Pre-PR aggregate (lint + unit tests + e2e shard coverage + i18n/lockfile "
"drift; **recommended**): `make check`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:14
msgid "Lint with auto-fix (also re-extracts i18n strings): `make check-style-fix`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:15
msgid "Lint only: `make check-style`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:16
msgid "All unit tests: `make test`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:17
msgid "Single Go test: `go test -v ./<pkg> -run TestName`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:18
msgid ""
"Build & deploy plugin to a running Mattermost (linux-amd64 only by "
"default): `make deploy` Set `MAKE_ALL_PLATFORMS=1` only if you're "
"deploying to a Mac- or Windows-native server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:20
msgid ""
"E2E (self-contained, no env setup needed; slow, defer to CI when "
"possible): `make e2e`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:21
msgid ""
"Single e2e spec: `cd e2e && npx playwright test tests/path/spec.ts "
"--reporter=list`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:22
msgid ""
"Prompt evals (non-interactive): `make evals-ci` Provider: "
"`LLM_PROVIDER=openai|anthropic|azure|openaicompatible|all make evals-ci` "
"Model: `ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929 make evals-ci`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:25
msgid ""
"Streaming benchmarks: `go test -bench=. -benchmem ./llm/... "
"./streaming/...`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:27
msgid ""
"When `make check` fails, run the underlying targets individually (`make "
"check-style`, `make test`, `make check-shards`, `make check-i18n`, `make "
"check-locks`) to isolate which step broke. CI runs the same drift checks;"
" if i18n or a lockfile is out of sync, those targets regenerate the file "
"in place — review and commit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:29
msgid "Repository layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:31
msgid "Most Go packages live at the **repo root**, not under `server/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:33
msgid "`server/` — plugin entrypoint, lifecycle, configuration adapter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:34
msgid "`api/`, `mmapi/` — HTTP handlers; Mattermost API wrappers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:35
msgid "`llm/` — LLM provider abstractions and provider implementations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:36
msgid ""
"`mcp/`, `mcpserver/` — MCP client; embedded/HTTP/stdio MCP servers and "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:37
msgid ""
"`format/` — formatting of Mattermost entities for LLM consumption (see "
"Conventions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:38
msgid ""
"Other top-level feature packages exist (e.g. `bots/`, `channels/`, "
"`threads/`, `meetings/`, `search/`, `embeddings/`, `streaming/`, "
"`toolrunner/`, `websearch/`, …). Read the package name and skim the "
"package source before assuming purpose — note in particular that both "
"`conversation/` and `conversations/` exist and are not the same."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:39
msgid "`config/` — plugin configuration types and migration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:40
msgid "`webapp/` — React/TypeScript UI bundle (`webapp/src/`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:41
msgid "`e2e/` — Playwright + Testcontainers end-to-end tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:42
msgid "`evals/`, `cmd/evalviewer/` — prompt evaluation harness and TUI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:43
msgid "`i18n/` — extracted translation strings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:44
msgid "`docs/` — user/admin docs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:45
msgid "`public/bridgeclient/` — separate Go module published for other plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:47
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:49
msgid ""
"Linters (golangci-lint, ESLint, gofmt/goimports, header check, "
"editorconfig) already enforce formatting, imports, error checking, "
"license headers, and indentation. The rules below are the ones a linter "
"cannot enforce."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:51
msgid "File names: `snake_case.go` / `snake_case.ts(x)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:52
msgid ""
"TypeScript/React: PascalCase components, strict typing, **always styled-"
"components**, never inline `style={{...}}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:53
msgid ""
"New user-facing strings must go through i18n (`make i18n-extract` picks "
"them up)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:54
msgid "Go tests must be table-driven when there is more than one case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:55
msgid ""
"Never introduce a new test/mocking library; prefer to test against real "
"implementations instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:56
msgid ""
"All formatting of Mattermost entities (posts, users, channels, teams, "
"members) for LLM consumption or tool output must go through the `format/`"
" package. Never `fmt.Sprintf` model types inline; add a formatter to "
"`format/` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:57
msgid ""
"E2E shard maintenance: when adding a new spec that should run in CI, "
"assign it in `e2e/scripts/ci-test-groups.mjs` in the same change. `make "
"check-shards` validates coverage and is part of `make check`. Mock/non-"
"real-api tests go in the lightest `e2e-shard-*` group; provider-backed "
"tests go in the matching `*-real*` group; balance by expected runtime, "
"not alphabetically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:58
msgid ""
"Test for behavior that could break due to a real bug. Before writing a "
"test ask: \"If this test fails, does it indicate a real bug in our "
"code?\" In particular, do not assert on implementation details like "
"validation order or which error appears first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:60
msgid "OpenTelemetry tracing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:62
msgid "The plugin emits OpenTelemetry traces. Agent-relevant rules:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:64
msgid ""
"**Thread `ctx context.Context` as the first parameter** through every "
"entry point → LLM call code path. Don't introduce `context.Background()` "
"shortcuts in production code; the request-scoped context is what makes "
"spans correlate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:65
msgid ""
"Existing spans live in `bifrost/` (LLM calls), `llm/tools.go`, "
"`conversations/tool_handling.go`, `mcp/`, `search/`, `websearch/`, and "
"`streaming/`. The `otelgin` middleware adds HTTP spans automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:66
msgid ""
"To add a span: `ctx, span := telemetry.Tracer().Start(ctx, \"span name\","
" trace.WithAttributes(...))`, then `defer span.End()`. Record errors with"
" `span.RecordError(err)` and `span.SetStatus(codes.Error, msg)`. Reuse "
"attribute keys from `telemetry/attributes.go` instead of inventing new "
"ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:67
msgid ""
"When a `*llm.Context` parameter would shadow the `context` package in the"
" same file, import `\"context\"` as `stdcontext`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:68
msgid ""
"Config fields (`TelemetryOutput`, `OpenTelemetryEndpoint`) and local "
"Tempo/Grafana setup live in `docs/admin_guide.md`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:70
msgid "Never do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:72
msgid ""
"Never edit `webapp/dist/`, `server/dist/`, or `dist/` — regenerate with "
"the build commands above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:73
msgid ""
"Never hand-edit `webapp/src/i18n/en.json` — `make check-style-fix` re-"
"extracts it from webapp source. Add the user-facing string at the call "
"site instead. (Server-side `i18n/en.json` is hand-curated; mmgotool "
"extraction doesn't apply to this repo's `nicksnyder/go-i18n` setup.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:74
msgid "Never push to `master`; open a PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:76
msgid "Gotchas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:78
msgid ""
"If `make install-go-tools` fails to build `mattermost-govet`, the pinned "
"commit is incompatible with the active Go toolchain. The Makefile prints "
"the exact fix: bump `MATTERMOST_GOVET_VERSION` in the Makefile to a newer"
" commit. This is a real problem to fix, not a warning to ignore."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:79
msgid ""
"`postgres/pgvector_test.go` boots its own pgvector container via "
"`testcontainers-go` (`pgvector/pgvector:pg17`); `go test ./postgres/...` "
"works on a fresh checkout as long as Docker is available. To run against "
"an existing pgvector instance for fast iteration, set "
"`PGVECTOR_TEST_DSN`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:80
msgid ""
"Plugin config is migrated to the plugin DB on activation. For automation,"
" read/write `GET`/`PUT /plugins/mattermost-ai/admin/config` rather than "
"patching the Mattermost server config."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:81
msgid ""
"The embedded MCP server requires `SiteURL` to be set on the Mattermost "
"server, and uses in-memory transport (no HTTP). On tool name collisions "
"across MCP servers, first-registered wins; later duplicates are skipped "
"with a warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/agents/AGENTS.md:82
msgid ""
"`public/bridgeclient/` is a separately published Go module, not HTTP "
"assets; `HAS_PUBLIC` is intentionally cleared in the Makefile."
msgstr ""

